  "S3": {
   "headline": "With five years of warning, first-years see a deadline they can work towards, so they save, retrain and learn the tools, though many feel the clock.",
   "whatTheyDo": [
    {
     "tag": "save-more",
     "text": "77% save, for example putting a hundred a month aside from shop wages or saving for a flat deposit."
    },
    {
     "tag": "retrain",
     "text": "54% add practical skills, such as learning basic wiring with an uncle at weekends or choosing hardware and electronics modules."
    },
    {
     "tag": "learn-ai",
     "text": "48% learn the tools, for example one new simulation tool each term or two AI coding tools over the next year."
    },
    {
     "tag": "change-job",
     "text": "31% line up placements, such as summer work on sites with an uncle's building firm."
    },
    {
     "tag": "keep-going",
     "text": "29% carry on, such as keeping weekend depot shifts through second year."
    }
   ],
   "whatTheySay": [
    "They say **five years is enough** if people start at once and don't waste it.",
    "Many tell friends to **learn a skill with their hands and one with their heads**.",
    "Some push for **paid retraining and rules** so firms still hire young people."
   ],
   "whatTheyThink": [
    "Many fear they will **graduate just as it arrives**, in the worst year to look for a first job.",
    "Several want a **plan B** now, such as a trade, a master's or a second path beside the degree.",
    "Some feel **hands-on work lasts a few years longer**, which feels both lucky and unfair."
   ],
   "howTheyFeel": [
    "**Anxious but driven**: 116 feel anxious and 111 uneasy, and only 15 are calm.",
    "They call it a **deadline or exam**: a clock is better than not knowing.",
    "Several say it's calmer than the AI by 2028 case, but **still a weight**."
   ],
   "differences": [
    {
     "group": "Adaptability",
     "text": "Adaptive first-years worry least (1.91 against 2.77 for resistant ones), and 69% of them look for side income."
    },
    {
     "group": "Money cushion",
     "text": "89% of thin-cushion students save more, against 64% of those with strong cushions."
    },
    {
     "group": "Outlook",
     "text": "73% of progressive first-years retrain, while 43% of traditional ones make family plans."
    }
   ],
   "quotes": [
    {
     "id": "U01-12213",
     "name": "Vera Costa",
     "text": "I think I'd be one of the people who can ride the wave rather than get hit by it, but I know that's not guaranteed."
    },
    {
     "id": "U01-21133",
     "name": "Sam Ibrahim",
     "text": "Two is a sprint and ten is a jog. Five is a proper run: you can plan and move."
    },
    {
     "id": "U01-12111",
     "name": "David Mensah",
     "text": "I'd rather be a qualified electrician with a computer science year behind me than a coder with a loan and no job"
    }
   ],
   "segments": {
    "least": {
